# The wave's two new landscapes, and the two things wrong with them: the salt
# flats clipped to paper wherever it met an older land, and glare was the one
# pressure the best legal kit could not answer; the scrapwood read as an
# ordinary wood with a pale pond in it, and its magnetism never let up.
#
# Each landscape at three zooms and three hours, both borders stood in and
# walked across, and a body standing in each with the best kit the game can
# make — put on through the slate's gear page with the real keys.
#   tools/tour.sh tours/salt-and-scrap.tour --seed=7 --hour=11 --weather=clear:0 \
#     --give=hat_brim:1,back_awning:1,mitts_corded:1,mod_foil:1
coast calm

# --- The flat: wide, at play, and close ---------------------------------------
place salt_flats
wait 2.0
zoom 20
wait 0.8
shot 01-flat-wide
zoom 12
wait 0.8
shot 02-flat-play
zoom 6
wait 0.8
shot 03-flat-close
zoom 12
hour 19.5
wait 1.6
shot 04-flat-dusk
hour 23
wait 1.6
shot 05-flat-night
hour 11
wait 1.2

# --- Glare with nothing on: the wall -----------------------------------------
await glare 20
await pressure_bites 20
shot 06-the-flat-bites

# --- And the kit that answers it, fitted on the slate -------------------------
# The brimmed hat goes on the head and the awning on the BACK: two slots, so
# glare is answerable at last without giving up the scanner lens for it.
tap pause
choose loadout
tap use
await app:loadout 8
shot 07-the-gear-page-bare
choose head
tap use
wait 0.4
choose back
tap use
wait 0.4
shot 08-a-brim-and-an-awning
tap pause
tap pause
await app:none 4
wait 2.5
await answered:glare 45
shot 09-the-flat-answered

# --- The wood: wide, at play, and close ---------------------------------------
place scrapwood
wait 2.0
zoom 20
wait 0.8
shot 10-wood-wide
zoom 12
wait 0.8
shot 11-wood-play
zoom 6
wait 0.8
shot 12-wood-close
zoom 12
hour 19.5
wait 1.6
shot 13-wood-dusk
hour 23
wait 1.6
shot 14-wood-night
hour 11
wait 1.6

# --- Magnetism, and the mitts with no iron in them ----------------------------
await magnetism 20
tap pause
choose loadout
tap use
await app:loadout 8
choose hands
tap use
wait 0.4
shot 15-nothing-on-the-hands-to-pull
tap pause
tap pause
await app:none 4
wait 1.5
shot 16-the-wood-answered

# --- What the wood is made of, at the scale a player meets it at --------------
# Close in: at play zoom a scrap tree is a crown with a line through it and a
# heap is a dark lump, and a frame that names a thing has to show it.
near scrap_tree
zoom 5
wait 1.2
shot 17-a-tree-grown-through-a-machine
near magnet_heap
wait 1.2
shot 18-filings-standing-on-end
zoom 12

# --- Both borders: stood in, then walked across -------------------------------
# The band has to carry two washes, two marks and two hatch hands. Neither side
# may clip to paper: a clipped wash holds no shade, no plate and no ink.
place coast-salt_flats
wait 2.2
shot 19-coast-meets-salt
walk 1,-1 2.5 run
wait 0.6
shot 20-coast-salt-crossed
place moss-scrapwood
wait 2.2
shot 21-moss-meets-scrapwood
walk 1,-1 2.5 run
wait 0.6
shot 22-moss-scrapwood-crossed
